Summary: Don't deadlock when a window's OpenGL context is updated from the main thread
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/). The code is the same
 in WineHQ 10.0 to master and in CrossOver 26.3.0 (checked 2026-11-25).
Why: macdrv_update_opengl_context updates the context through
 OnMainThread, which queues the block on the main thread's run loop and
 waits for it. OnMainThread doesn't check whether it's already on the main
 thread, and the content view's viewWillDraw calls
 macdrv_update_opengl_context on the main thread for GL contexts added while
 the view wasn't on screen. When that context has no latent view left, the
 block waits behind the main thread itself, and the main thread hangs for
 good, with every other thread that needs it (wined3d's command stream thread
 in wglSwapBuffers, for one). Update the context directly when already on
 the main thread, as the function's other branches already do.
 Samples of the hung White Wolf Queen showed the main thread in
 viewWillDraw -> macdrv_update_opengl_context -> OnMainThread, entered from
 AppKit's fullscreen transition, and wined3d's thread in wglSwapBuffers
 waiting for the main thread.
Programs: White Wolf Queen (Big Fish trial): hangs as its window goes into
 its fullscreen Space on macOS 26 (4 of 7 launches on builds 2 and 4)
Seen on: macOS 26 (White Wolf Queen, 11.22 builds 2 and 4, Second Chance
 integration runs: 4 hangs in 7 launches)
Uncertain: how the main thread reached this branch: a pending context
 normally still has its latent view. Most likely a GL thread consumed it at
 the same moment (the race winemac-serialise-gl-context-changes closes).
Related: winemac-serialise-gl-context-changes,
 winemac-gl-context-dealloc-off-main-thread; the same viewWillDraw and GL
 thread interplay
No test: timing only: it takes a context that's pending on a view with no
 latent view, which so far has only happened in the middle of a fullscreen
 Space transition
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-17: built in macfixes-11.22-build5; the regression
 suite passes. Confirmed: White Wolf Queen's Big Fish trial on macOS 26 ran
 10 of 10 launches without a hang (4 hangs in 7 on builds 2 and 4).
 11.21: 2026-11-17: built in macfixes-11.21-build6; the regression suite
 passes. No game run on 11.21.
 10.0: 2026-11-17: built in macfixes-10.0-build6; the regression suite
 passes. No game run on 10.0.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
index c15aefe..5488840 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -308,6 +308,13 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
                 [context clearDrawableLeavingSurfaceOnScreen];
                 context.view = view;
             }
+            else if ([NSThread isMainThread])
+            {
+                /* From the content view's viewWillDraw, which runs on the main
+                 * thread: OnMainThread would queue the block behind itself and
+                 * wait for ever. */
+                [context update];
+            }
             else OnMainThread(^{
                 [context update];
             });
